      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be nice for whitelisting, because as far as I know, the only way that is exposed to Udon for identifying players is the display name, but if the player changed their display name, that won't work for them anymore until the whitelist is updated. Unless you use some kind of Persistance to fix this issue, there is no other workaround with that. Though this could be a problem for Blacklisting as someone else also pointed out, this could be a definitive way to ensure a player doesn't lose access to areas, like from supporting a creators patreon to access special areas, or whitelisted features like a infinite ammo in weapons in game worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
