      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a feature that is urgently needed. I am sick and tired of reediting the Patreon lists all the time with the users swapping their names every 30 (with VRC+?) / 90 days with some silly and most of the time annoying ASCII symbols, which I am tired to fiddle out, which one of the arabic, kanji or whatever symbols they used, as they look way different outside of the VRC's font renderer.\n\nBesides of the obvious benefit of saving us a lot of work, it would also mean, no one would be able to impersonate someone else in the system. I don't want people to use my admin-panel in my worlds to gain access to critical functions and benefits, if they find a way to exploit the displayname fetcher, which may happen, as people are able to inject their scummy scripts into worlds like FISH! (VRC's cashcow) and others to have purchased-item benefits for no cost.\n\nBut VRC employees do simply not care about world developers, as long as they are not making them a ton of money. I was asking for years to expose the damn radial expression menu to Udon, because of the world menu I've created, that triggers while the radial menu is being present. It just annoys me. It is not professional, nor do I have the time to figure out what restrictions Udon will throw at me all the time, when I try 10 different approaches of pseudo-registering the expression menu popup. I am tired of it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-09T01:16:15.701Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Now that web connectivity will likely require some form of consent from the user when using Udon, I think it's a reasonable request to ask for an actual unique user ID that we can use to identify users. This could be used to do things like enable a debug console in the world, or when web connectivity is back, save progress or settings in a world.\nRight now people are using display names as \"unique\" identifiers which isn't good and already has issues since it's a display name. One issue is https://vrchat.canny.io/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/onplayerjoined-doesnt-get-full-displayname-for-steam-users \nAnother issue is that \"special\" characters like \".\" get replaced in the display name with lookalikes which breaks string comparisons. \n\nRelying on display name to \"uniquely\" identify people will become more prevalent as time goes on and people make commonly used systems that depend on them. You should expose this sooner rather than later to avoid this issue.\n\nThe potential for abuse is obviously possible, but there's no reason to kneecap the systems and introduce potential issues by leaving only display names visible. Right now I can reasonably target people with just their display names, it's just possible that there will be some more people with the same name that get targeted. Worlds abusing names to harass people is something that should be reported on a world basis.",
